From 70117bd22759d818ecac09398159f8eaf44ec790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:06:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/46] video: fbdev: add native I2C and LDO cold stage

Add a root-only, write-once cold_init control for ABI-v3 cold probe.
Reclaim I2C0 with the pinned ESP-IDF v6.0.1 clock, timing, GPIO,
and IOMUX configuration. Reissue the ACKed PWM-zero, reset-prepare,
and reset-assert command sequence without claiming external readback.

Calculate the 2500-mV LDO3 settings from silicon eFuse calibration and
apply the IDF voltage, owner, ripple-suppression, and enable sequence.
Verify the programmed fields, then release and gate I2C0 before entering
LDO_READY. Leave the DSI and GDMA blocks reset and clocks disabled.

On any failure, best-effort reissue PWM-zero and reset-assert, clear LDO
XPD, gate I2C0, and enter FAILED_QUIESCENT with retry limited to reboot.
Do not register fbdev, backlight, or an IRQ in this stage.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
